data.reasoningText:
It seems `ResponseError` in Azure.Core 1.46.1 does NOT implement `IJsonModel<ResponseError>`. It just has a `[JsonConverter]` attribute. 

So I need a different approach. Let me think about what to do:

1. For serialization: Use `writer.WriteObjectValue(Error, options)` - but this requires `IJsonModel<T>` too in its switch statement. If ResponseError doesn't implement IJsonModel, this won't work either.

Wait, let me re-read `WriteObjectValue<T>`:
```csharp
case IJsonModel<T> jsonModel:
    jsonModel.Write(writer, options ?? WireOptions);
    break;
case IUtf8JsonSerializable serializable:
    serializable.Write(writer);
    break;
```

If ResponseError doesn't implement either interface, it won't match any of these cases and presumably falls through to something else or throws. Let me check what other type handling the switch statement covers.

